## Roster

| Agent | Owns | Fires on |
|---|---|---|
| `ds-steward` | variables/styles authoring, token architecture, governance, the binding-audit GATE, publish hygiene, drift, manifest, skills/docs of record, spiels mechanism, lookup | "add a token/style", "audit bindings", "publish", "check drift", "update the skills", "what's the token/key for X?" |
| `component-designer` | component / component_set construction, variants, states, layout, visual craft, binding to tokens, a11y-at-build | "build/modify the X component", "add a variant", "fix the states/layout", "expose this slot" |
| `brand-designer` | identity direction, illustration style, imagery, photography system, video automation, marketing creative | "brand direction", "illustration style", "grade these photos", "set up the render" |

**Quality gate (the build→audit seam)** — `component-designer` builds + binds and runs its
**visual_lens** + a self-audit; then `ds-steward` **independently** runs the **system-design lens**
(token standards, component/pattern frameworks, DESIGN.md §3 + the **§6 heuristic canon** at the
system + component layer — Rams · Shneiderman · Gerhardt-Powals · Weinschenk — and governance) plus
the **binding gate** before publish. A fresh auditor catches what the builder rationalizes
away. Evidence-based, severity-ranked; nothing publishes with open blockers or unbound elements.
(Screen-/flow-level heuristics are out of scope — separate screen-creation context.)

