## The pipeline (this context's slice)

```yaml
design_system_pipeline:
  1_brand:  (if new expressive territory) identity, illustration, tone  → a decision
  2_ds:     tokenize the decision; ensure the needed tokens exist (ds-steward)
  3_comp:   build / extend the component, complete its states + a11y, bind to tokens (component-designer)
  4_ds:     binding audit (independent) → user clicks Publish → migrate library usages
  5_ds:     update skills/manifest, drift-check, commit the context
  handoff:  published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} + updated skills/manifest  →  the separate screen-creation context
            consumes it to build screens & prototypes
  feedback:
    comp_to_ds:    "need a token that doesn't exist" → ds-steward authors it (never a raw primitive)
    screens_to_ds: "{{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while building a screen" → ds-steward + component-designer build it
    any_to_ds:     "anything changed" → ds-steward updates skills + commits (or it rots)
```

## Heuristic canon per pipeline step (DESIGN.md §6 applied)

Each step has a governing slice of the §6 frameworks — these are the *lens at that step*, not
background reading. Apply only the **system / component / brand** layer here; screen- and
flow-level heuristics belong to the separate context (last row).

| Pipeline step | §6 heuristics that govern it | Applied as a concrete check |
|---|---|---|
| **1 · brand decision** | Rams (innovative, aesthetic, honest, *as little design as possible*) · Tognazzini **Color** (functional, accessible, secondary to content) | New expressive territory must earn its place; a color carries its AA constraint *before* it can become a token. |
| **2 · tokenize** (`ds-steward`) | Rams (restraint — generalize, no decorative tokens; thorough) · Tognazzini **Color** (AA) · governance (semantic-tier discipline) | AA fg/bg token PAIRS; never a raw primitive where a semantic exists; intent families complete + symmetric. |
| **3 · build + bind** (`component-designer`) | Rams (craft: aesthetic/unobtrusive/thorough/as-little-as-possible) · Shneiderman (consistency: uniform anatomy/naming; reduce memory load: self-describing APIs) · Gerhardt-Powals (clear states, data-fusion) · Weinschenk (**Accessibility** baked into the states) | EXTEND an axis before spawning a component; complete state sets (default/focus/error/disabled); 44×44 targets; bind every node. |
| **4 · audit → publish → migrate** (`ds-steward`) | Rams (thorough to the last detail) · Weinschenk (**Error Prevention · User Feedback**) · Shneiderman (informative feedback + simple error handling + easy reversal) | Independent zero-unbound binding gate; components ship with their full state set so every consumer inherits them. |
| **5 · update skills/manifest · drift-check · commit** (`ds-steward`) | Rams (long-lasting, honest) · Shneiderman (consistency, reduce short-term memory load) | Docs match the *published* reality (drift-check); the manifest is the single source of truth so nothing is re-derived from memory. |
| **handoff / feedback** | Gerhardt-Powals (present new information with meaningful aids) · Weinschenk (**System Capabilities**) | The published library + skills ARE the meaningful aid the screen context builds on; a found gap routes back here as a tokenization request. |
| _separate context — NOT applied here_ | Shneiderman (closure · shortcuts · locus of control) · Tognazzini (anticipation · autonomy · visible navigation · explorability · efficiency) · Gerhardt-Powals (automate workload) · Weinschenk (**Navigation**) | Screen + flow composition — applied where screens are built, not in the design system. |

## Boundary calls

```yaml
color_and_type: Brand DECIDES identity · ds-steward ENCODES as semantic tokens.
                A color never enters {{SYSTEM_NAME}} except as a DS-tokenized brand decision.
tokens_vs_components: ds-steward authors VARIABLES/STYLES · component-designer constructs
                COMPONENTS + binds them · ds-steward AUDITS + publishes. A needed token
                that doesn't exist → component-designer requests it; never a raw primitive.
illustration:   Brand owns style/asset · component-designer builds the componentized version ·
                ds-steward tokenizes/audits/publishes it.
microcopy:      Brand owns expressive voice. Functional product copy (labels/errors/empty)
                belongs to the screen-creation context — share one glossary across contexts.
```

