## Slash commands (thin wrappers — they delegate, they don't duplicate)

| Command | Delegates to | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `/design-system-check [target]` | `ds-steward` | run the system-design lens |
| `/binding-audit [component]` | `ds-steward` | binding-completeness gate |
| `/drift-check [actual.json]` | `ds-steward` | manifest vs actual drift |

Each command body only *invokes the agent* — the workflow lives in **one** place. The catch: if a
command restates the audit logic, the same workflow now exists in two places (command + agent) and
keeping them in sync is the exact drift problem this repo exists to kill. So the only safe command is
a thin one that delegates. Add new commands the same way: thin, delegating — never duplicate the logic.

