## Separate context — screen creation + live prototyping

By design, this context is **design-system only**. Two concerns deliberately live in a **different
context** (`{{STUDIO_REPO}}` — a separate repo / session / agent set), so they don't pull
screen-building or coded-prototype tooling into the design-system window:

- **Screen creation** — composing {{SYSTEM_NAME}} into pixel-perfect consumer screens (the consumer file
  `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}`), plus the UX definition that precedes it (flows, IA, state matrices,
  specs, functional microcopy). The `ux-designer` + `ui-designer` + `flow-reviewer` +
  `consumer-migrator` agents (+ `/design-review`, `/consumer-audit`, `/rebind` and the
  screen-review / rebind skills) live in **`../{{STUDIO_REPO}}/`**, not here.
- **Live prototyping** — coded prototypes (React/Vite, instrumented for usability testing), in
  `../{{STUDIO_REPO}}/`. Driven by the usability-prototype skill / builder agent, not these.
- **Consume-verification** — after a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish, the studio context runs the rebind /
  `consumer-migrator` procedure to swap stale consumer instances onto the fresh main + confirm the
  change is actually used downstream.

**Handoff across the boundary:** `ds-steward` publishes {{SYSTEM_NAME}} + updates `skills/` + `manifest/`;
the screen-creation context consumes the published library to build. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while
building a screen comes back here as a tokenization/component request — `ds-steward` builds and
publishes it, the screen context waits or stubs. `DESIGN.md` is shared ground truth that both read.

---

## Relationship to the bootstrap

`CLAUDE.md` / `CONTEXT.md` still boot the session with project facts, file keys, version, and
preferences. `DESIGN.md` is the design-principles source the agents read. These three agents
(`ds-steward`, `component-designer`, `brand-designer`) are the execution specialists this context
delegates to after boot. The canonical workflows live **inside the agents** (Claude Code only) — there
are no separate `kickoff-prompts/*.md` to keep in sync; the agents read `skills/*.md` + `DESIGN.md` +
the manifest for the detail.

> Note on surface: per the repo README, {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Figma *writes* run through the Desktop Bridge. If
> your Claude Code has a Figma write MCP wired in, `ds-steward` executes directly; if not, it acts as a
> planner that emits the `use_figma` script + audit checklist for a bridge session.
